      "text_raw": "Some of the specifications\nare collected here.\nIts FOM is not poor, as\nit is 56 MHzpF/mA. This\nshows again that duplicat-\ning the input stage of a two-\nstage opamp is more accept-\nable from the point of view\nof power consumption.\nThe input g /I is\nm1 DS1\nabout 20 V−1, which shows\nthat the transistor is in weak\ninversion. Because of the\nlow currents used, the equiv-\nalent input noise is rather\nhigh.\nIn weak inversion, the transistors have large sizes. The offset is fairly small. The change of\noffset is fairly small as well!",
      "text": "Some of the specifications are collected here. Its FOM is not poor, as it is 56 MHzpF/mA. This shows again that duplicating the input stage of a twostage opamp is more acceptable from the point of view of power consumption. The input g /I is m1 DS1 about 20 V−1, which shows that the transistor is in weak inversion. Because of the low currents used, the equivalent input noise is rather high. In weak inversion, the transistors have large sizes. The offset is fairly small. The change of offset is fairly small as well!"
